; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Power by Halves
; CATEGORY: Recursion
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     recursion, powers, multiplication, efficiency
; SUMMARY:  Raises a number to a power two ways, one multiplication at a time and by halving the exponent, and counts the work.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   2 to the power 10 means ten 2s multiplied together.
;   SLOWPOWER uses the rule  b^n = b x b^(n-1), so it needs n steps.
;   FASTPOWER notices that b^10 = b^5 x b^5. Work out b^5 once and
;   square it. When the exponent is odd, peel off one b first. Each
;   step halves the exponent, so even b^1000 takes only a few steps.
;   Both versions print an indented line for each call they make.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   1. Press Run and compare the two traces.
;   2. Put a breakpoint on the first line of FASTPOWER,
;        if :n = 0 [output 1]
;      run with F5, and keep pressing F5. In the Variables panel watch
;      :n go 13, 6, 3, 1, 0. Halving reaches 0 very quickly.
;   3. Do the same in SLOWPOWER and count the presses.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a recursive rule with a base case of n = 0
;   * splitting a problem in half instead of shrinking it by one
;   * EVEN and ODD with REMAINDER
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change the numbers in the last lines: try 3 to the 20.
;   * How many steps does fastpower need for 2 to the 1000? Count them,
;     do not print the answer (it is too big).
; ============================================================

; Each level of the trace is indented two more spaces than the last.
to slowpower :b :n :indent
  print (word :indent :b "^ :n)
  if :n = 0 [output 1]
  output :b * slowpower :b :n - 1 word :indent "|  |
end

to fastpower :b :n :indent
  print (word :indent :b "^ :n)
  if :n = 0 [output 1]
  ; HALF is the answer for half the exponent, found only ONCE.
  ; Calling fastpower twice here would throw away all the savings.
  localmake "half fastpower :b int :n / 2 word :indent "|  |
  if (remainder :n 2) = 0 [output :half * :half]
  ; odd exponent: one extra b is left over
  output :b * :half * :half
end

print [Slow way, one multiplication per step:]
print sentence [Answer:] slowpower 2 13 "
print []
print [Fast way, halving the exponent:]
print sentence [Answer:] fastpower 2 13 "
print []
print [Check with the built-in POWER:]
print power 2 13
